<title>BELGIUM: Europe majority share in Brussels 96 cargo traffic.</title>
<headline>Europe majority share in Brussels 96 cargo traffic.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Europe accounted for the majority of global air cargo traffic (imports and exports) handled at Brussels airport in 1996, airport authority figures showed.</p>
<p>Last year, Brussels at 456,231 tonnes recorded a seven percent increase in cargo throughput on 1995 levels.</p>
<p>Market share of global cargo traffic handled at Brussels airport in 1996, by geographical region, with 1995 market share in brackets:</p>
<p>    REGION	    TONNAGE  '96 RANK '95 RANK</p>
<p>    Domestic		 215    0.05   (0.05)</p>
<p>    Europe	     224,355   49.2   (45.6)</p>
<p>    North America     92,028   20.2   (20.6)</p>
<p>    Latin America	3,249    0.7    (0.7)</p>
<p>    Middle East	 56,432   12.4   (13.9)</p>
<p>    Australasia	 49,276   10.8   (11.7)</p>
<p>    Africa		30,676    6.7    (7.4)</p>
<p>Total  456,231 tonnes</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
<p>- www.racs.com</p>
